Subject: the arena load path: a root module links where boot2 placed it

30 section 2 patch 2 (S4-01), contract C4-4 version 2 section 4.
dlm_load_mem(name, p, len, bss) loads a root-class module from its file
bytes in the arena: no path, no file read, no hash (the root pass checks
the CRC-32 against the directory).  Its allocated PROGBITS sections are
relocated where they lie (each at an offset that is a multiple of its
alignment, at most 16); NOBITS and COMMON go into the zeroed tail boot2
reserved behind the file, and a layout larger than the reserve is
ENOLOAD.  The image is that one span, so the range checks stay as they
are; nothing is allocated for it or freed.  Root class is accepted only
from the arena, and only root class there; a dependency must already be
linked.  The state harness loads modules with .bss, a common and data
relocated against both, and each refusal.

